  "comment": "X-02 §2: ListenOrigin's two checks. 'form' is ListenOrigin::parse: 'result' is 'accepted' (then 'origin' is the canonical serialization, which Display and serde give back) or the refusal's OriginError::code(). The canonical form is the WHATWG URL origin serialization, refused and never rewritten when the input isn't already in it. 'whatwg' is what a WHATWG parser gives for the input (null when it throws), recorded from Node 26 with: node -e 'console.log(new URL(process.argv[1]).origin)' '<input>'. Every accepted row agrees with it. A refused row whose 'whatwg' equals its input (less a trailing /) is one where ListenOrigin is stricter than browsers, by decision; it says why in 'stricter_than_browsers'. 'fit' is ListenOrigin::check(scheme, address, port): 'result' is 'accepted' or the OriginError::code() of the first failed check, in the order scheme, port, loopback bind address, bound literal. Either step's refusal makes a stored configuration origin_invalid.",
